    "narrative": "The Austin Waves roster faces a challenging slate today, largely dictated by facing Gavin Williams, whose 2.95 xERA suppresses the ceiling for our primary middle-infield cohort. **Miguel Vargas** leads our output at 42.07, clinging to a starting spot primarily due to his assumed leadoff status. While his base projection is solid, the matchup against Williams demands caution; he remains a marginal play, though his 0.378 xwOBA suggests he is the most capable of navigating this tough SP pairing. **Sam Antonacci** follows closely at 40.83, benefiting from a +7% platoon edge that keeps his score above our 40-point threshold. Despite the pitching hurdle, **Sam Antonacci** maintains value in a favorable batting order position, though we are essentially chasing volume over efficiency in this matchup.\n\n**Brayan Rocchio** rounds out our active starters at 40.63, narrowly crossing the floor threshold despite hitting at the bottom of the order. The risk here is significant; hitting #9 against a functional arm like Sean Burke (3.79 xERA) limits his R/RBI potential. Among our core, **Luis Robert Jr.** remains sidelined on the IL, while elite assets like **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Gunnar Henderson** provide zero utility today due to team off-days. With **Andy Pages**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Jordan Westburg** currently outside the active rotation, the decision to run with **Brayan Rocchio** over lower-tier reserves was purely based on his consistent role in the lineup, though the proximity of his score to the bench threshold is a concern. We are monitoring the official lineups closely for **Miguel Vargas**, **Brayan Rocchio**, and **Sam Antonacci**; any downward shift in their expected batting order would likely trigger a benching to preserve our game caps, as the current environment offers little upside against the scheduled pitching.",
